{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqay3tl876m","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Autowire is direction blind: results get wired as context for their own producers","summary":"Finding from judge drain passes (2026-06-12, sonnet): the dominant prune pattern in the edge backlog is WRONG-DIRECTION autowire edges — e.g. note-mq7iakmckgt (an onboarding-plateau RESULT note) carried 7 context edges pointing at the tasks/notes that PRODUCED it. Root cause: cosine autowire is direction-blind (similarity is symmetric), so a result gets wired as a prerequisite for its own inputs. Slice evidence: pass 2 pruned 14/15 edges (93%), pass 1 pruned 5/11 (45%) — the autowire 0.25-threshold firehose is mostly noise that the judge then pays sonnet tokens to clean. Improvement candidate (not yet tasked): add a direction/recency guard to autowire — a note created after a task completes should not become that task's context provider; provenance belongs to wires_to, not cosine. Would cut queue growth at the source, same pattern as the write-time dup guard. Also: 5 more dup-clusters surfaced this pass, all correctly judged DISTINCT (false-positive merges — different files, different probe IDs) — the 0.70 write-guard + judge-gray-zone split keeps behaving as designed.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T13:11:37.868Z","vec":[-0.0903758630156517,-0.03968324512243271,0.0063020940870046616,0.010258585214614868,0.03300375118851662,0.024359598755836487,0.002474758541211486,-0.006156786810606718,0.02813953533768654,-0.027456704527139664,0.022839901968836784,-0.013608373701572418,-0.006596253253519535,-0.036949459463357925,-0.10506203770637512,-0.06150737404823303,0.057183243334293365,-0.06724747270345688,0.0001300208386965096,-0.06365901976823807,0.0041984315030276775,-0.0028564543463289738,0.040942028164863586,0.0069191292859613895,0.08549346029758453,-0.06000553071498871,-0.015876950696110725,0.006813820451498032,-0.011912142857909203,-0.08196795731782913,-0.08860038965940